t's participants on the seams that already fire the text, with the chat line kept as the subtitle track throughout. The Wither speaks its ten shipped taunt lines on real eats (the picked line's clip, index-aligned in wither.taunt-sounds, under the same 25s cooldown); the dragon speaks at battle registration, at the flip, at its per-phase milestone beats (the phase-2 50% stamp has its own crystals line) and at its phase-2 add waves; the elder guardians speak at first damage, at their beats, at the trio relay and as the last door standing; the Warden speaks at first damage, on its sonic booms (rate-limited to the taunt cooldown, two clips alternating) and at its beats; and every chapter speaks its verdict line as it falls. Voice is fail-soft throughout - a missing clip is chat-only and logged once, and a playback failure can never strand the fight event it rides. The six raid clips ride the packs inert in this build; their speaker is the GuildGate narrator and their playback waits for a later GuildGate packet, so no raid key exists here. 0.5.3 files the Item 39 Warden retune as the shipped behavior, test-proven in the retune rounds on the bracket gear (Protection IV netherite tank, Protection IV diamond others) - the warden's pressure settles at its natural strength (warden.pressure outgoing-multiplier 1.0 and ramp-max 1.5, shipped as the defaults in place of 1.25 and 2.0) and its sonic boom is exempt from the pressure scale (the per-chapter key pressure.apply-to-sonic-boom, default false), so the boom reads its exact vanilla 15 HP at minute zero, mid-ramp and past the cap while melee keeps the full ramp (past-cap melee base 67.5, about 18 HP through Protection IV netherite - hard hits, no one-shots); the exemption is the Warden chapter's alone, the key set true restores the pre-0.5.3 scaled boom, and every other chapter, the voice, the sprinkle, the crystal flip and the display scale are exactly as 0.5.2 shipped them. 0.5.4 is the elder sprinkle melee fix - the elder